<title>FRANCE: Paris airports' Jan-May export cargo up two pct.</title>
<headline>Paris airports' Jan-May export cargo up two pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-May 1997 export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 235,101 tonnes, up two percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The Paris airports' January-May 1997 export traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on January-May 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>    Domestic		 17,056	down 10.6 percent</p>
<p>    European Union	 29,168	up    8.8</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe	  5,709	 up   10.8</p>
<p>    North Africa	   4,392	 up    2.0</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa  18,676	 up    1.6</p>
<p>    North America	 65,108	 up    5.7</p>
<p>    French territories  10,880     down    1.7</p>
<p>    Latin America	 12,833	 up    3.3</p>
<p>    Middle East	   23,147	 up    0.3</p>
<p>    Far East		48,132     down    0.7</p>
<p>    Total		  235,101	 up    2.0</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
